## 7. Worked Example: Intelligent Context Stewardship

### 7.1 The originating observation

The operator recognized that CCV currently benefits from his unusually disciplined manual curation.

He repeatedly decides:

* what is load-bearing;
* what belongs in the active thread;
* what should be compressed;
* what should be archived;
* what is only a seed;
* what belongs outside ELT;
* and where a productive segue has completed its work.

The next design question was:

> How can this process become more automated for operators who do not curate context as instinctively?

# Intelligent Context Stewardship

### 7.2 Core idea

> **Preserve value without preserving heat.**

A concept can be worth saving without remaining active in attention.

The system should distinguish:

[
\text{worth preserving}
\neq
\text{worth keeping hot}
]

### 7.3 Five-state classification

| State        | Meaning                                                | Action                              |
| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------- |
| **Hold**     | Load-bearing for the current task                      | Keep salient                        |
| **Compress** | Relevant, but full detail is no longer needed          | Preserve a short summary            |
| **Archive**  | Valuable for later, but inactive now                   | Move into a seed or project archive |
| **Yield**    | No longer useful enough to preserve                    | Release                             |
| **Escalate** | Material unresolved issue that may alter the synthesis | Return to active attention          |

### 7.4 Why this matters

Long-context failure is not only forgetting.

It is also failure to release.

A thread becomes less useful when too many items remain simultaneously active:

* resolved questions;
* repeated caveats;
* expired assumptions;
* abandoned branches;
* half-developed tangents;
* and ideas that are useful but not currently relevant.

Intelligent Context Stewardship helps preserve CCV while preventing context sludge.

