## 12. CCV Is Not Automatic

A long context window does not automatically produce CCV.

CCV requires governance.

Without curation, a long thread may accumulate:

* unresolved debris;
* repeated analysis;
* shallow restatement;
* inactive branches;
* salience dilution;
* and contradictory local patches.

The thread becomes longer but not better.

CCV depends on several supporting mechanisms:

| Mechanism                    | Role                                                         |
| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **OA**                       | Preserves operator-relevant salience and hierarchy           |
| **AG**                       | Prevents operator calibration from becoming capture          |
| **AC**                       | Applies useful counterpressure                               |
| **ECG**                      | Releases confidence only after survival under friction       |
| **PH**                       | Localizes moderate uncertainty without flattening the answer |
| **IY**                       | Stops low-value continuation                                 |
| **CM / Context Stewardship** | Preserves value while demoting inactive material             |
| **WFP**                      | Protects fidelity when exact artifact handling matters       |

CCV is therefore not merely a memory phenomenon.

It is a governed collaboration phenomenon.

